  {
   "id": 673581,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Postpartum depression is a serious condition that can impact both the caregiver and the newborn. Define postpartum depression and discuss the common symptoms, as well as how it differs from the “baby blues.” Analyze the risk factors that contribute to postpartum depression and propose strategies that health-care providers and loved ones can use to support new parents. In your discussion, consider both medical interventions and community-based support systems. Additionally, explore the importance of reducing stigma around mental health struggles in new parents and the cultural factors that may influence how postpartum depression is recognized and treated.",
